        "is_free": false,
        "controller_support": "full",
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.poster.avif?t=1763120663\" width=640 height=200 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.webm?t=1763120663\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.mp4?t=1763120663\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rated among the <strong>top 1% of games in the 2025 GMTK Game Jam</strong>, Sisyphus Is a Bug is a <strong>knowledgevania</strong> about a dung beetle's eternal punishment... now expanded with a <strong>new campaign</strong>!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sisyphus, the dung beetle, happily rolling his ball of dung, found himself among the gods in Mount Olympus. Zeus, upon seeing the wretched creature dirtying his marble halls, condemns Sisyphus to roll his ball of dung up the mountain every day, for the rest of his life. That is, unless he can reach Olympus before the sun sets...</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Reach</strong> Olympus in 60 seconds... or fall down the mountain and do it all over again</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Learn</strong> movement tricks to help you overcome obstacles quickly</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Earn</strong> achievements along the way</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discover</strong> a brand new campaign exclusive to the Steam release!</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.poster.avif?t=1763120663\" width=640 height=200 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.webm?t=1763120663\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3971000/extras/bf7a41c0b87ca48919813217ddfe33b2.mp4?t=1763120663\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rated among the <strong>top 1% of games in the 2025 GMTK Game Jam</strong>, Sisyphus Is a Bug is a <strong>knowledgevania</strong> about a dung beetle's eternal punishment... now expanded with a <strong>new campaign</strong>!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sisyphus, the dung beetle, happily rolling his ball of dung, found himself among the gods in Mount Olympus. Zeus, upon seeing the wretched creature dirtying his marble halls, condemns Sisyphus to roll his ball of dung up the mountain every day, for the rest of his life. That is, unless he can reach Olympus before the sun sets...</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Reach</strong> Olympus in 60 seconds... or fall down the mountain and do it all over again</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Learn</strong> movement tricks to help you overcome obstacles quickly</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Earn</strong> achievements along the way</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discover</strong> a brand new campaign exclusive to the Steam release!</p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "As punishment for dirtying Olympus's marble halls, Sisyphus, the dung beetle, must push his ball of dung up and down Mount Olympus every day, for the rest of his life. That is, unless he can complete the seemingly impossible task of reaching Olympus before the sun sets",
        "supported_languages": "English, Portuguese - Brazil",
